          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "lineage": "Akania",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "An extinct fossil-leaf species of Akaniaceae (order Brassicales) described by Romero & Hickey (1976) from a leaf impression in the La Huitrera Formation near Laguna del Hunco, Chubut Province, Patagonian Argentina (early Eocene, ~52-47 Ma). With A. patagonica it documents that Akaniaceae, today restricted to eastern Australia, were widespread in the Southern Hemisphere during the Paleogene.",
