          "name": "Akania patagonica Gandolfo et al., 1988",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "lineage": "Akania",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "An extinct fossil-leaf species of Akaniaceae (order Brassicales) named by Gandolfo, Dibbern & Romero (1988) from Paleocene-Eocene sediments of Patagonia, known from the Huitrera Formation including the Laguna del Hunco and Rio Pichileufu early-Eocene floras. The leaf fossils support a formerly broad Gondwanan distribution of the family and close Paleogene links between the South American and Australian floras.",
